 "result_text": "`notification.add` and `notification.update` should now send valid JSON. I haven't run the tests or made a real API call.\n\nThe cause was in `RachioObject._request`. It passed the payload dict straight to `requests` as `data=`, so `requests` sent it form-encoded rather than as JSON. The server then failed to parse `device` as a JSON token, which is the error in the issue.\n\nThe fix, in `rachiopy/rachioobject.py`, serializes the body with `json.dumps` whenever it isn't already a string or bytes. I made it there rather than in `notification.py` because the `zone`, `device` and `schedulerule` calls pass dict payloads the same way. They should now be sent as JSON as well.",
